/                   Root of everything
├── /bin            Essential user binaries (ls, cp, bash) – available in rescue mode
├── /sbin           System admin binaries (fdisk, iptables, systemctl)
├── /etc            ALL config files (no binaries!)
│   ├── /etc/fstab          Mount points
│   ├── /etc/passwd         User accounts
│   ├── /etc/shadow         Password hashes
│   ├── /etc/hosts          Local DNS overrides
│   ├── /etc/systemd/       Service units & targets
│   └── /etc/default/grub   GRUB config source
├── /dev            Device files (disks, terminals, null)
│   ├── /dev/sda, /dev/vda  Disks
│   ├── /dev/tty1-6         Virtual consoles
│   └── /dev/null           Data sink
├── /proc           Kernel/process info (virtual, RAM-only)
│   ├── /proc/cpuinfo       CPU details
│   ├── /proc/meminfo       Memory stats
│   └── /proc/cmdline       Boot parameters used
├── /sys            Hardware/kernel interface (virtual)
│   └── /sys/class/net/     Network interfaces (you used this!)
├── /tmp            Temporary files (cleared on reboot)
├── /var            Variable data that changes during runtime
│   ├── /var/log/           Logs (journal, syslog, auth.log)
│   ├── /var/lib/           App state (dpkg, systemd, databases)
│   └── /var/cache/         Cached data (apt, etc.)
├── /home           User home directories (/home/os)
├── /root           Root user’s home (NOT /)
├── /boot           Bootloader + kernel + initrd
│   ├── vmlinuz-*           Kernel images
│   ├── initrd.img-*        Initramfs
│   └── grub/               GRUB config & modules
├── /usr            Read-only user programs & data
│   ├── /usr/bin/           Non-essential user binaries
│   ├── /usr/sbin/          Non-essential admin binaries
│   ├── /usr/lib/           Libraries
│   └── /usr/share/         Docs, icons, locales
├── /opt            Optional/third-party software (e.g., /opt/homebrew)
├── /srv            Service data (web, ftp – rarely used)
├── /media          Auto-mounted removable media (USB, CD)
└── /mnt            Manual mount point for temp filesystems